<!--
    THE EIGHTH DAY - quests.xml
    ===========================
    The Provings. Six chains of three, one per Calling.

    A Calling is EARNED, not bought. Each Proving makes you do the discipline's
    actual work before it opens up, so the Ironmonger has run a bloomery before
    they can perk into alloying, and the Marshal has run out of ammunition at
    least once before anybody hands them a belt-fed gun.

    THE ONE RULE THIS FILE MUST NEVER BREAK
    =======================================
    No objective may require anything gated behind a Calling. The Proving is how
    you earn the Calling, so requiring its own output is a deadlock that a player
    cannot see coming and cannot escape. Every id below is either vanilla or
    craftable with no perk requirement - check this again every time you touch it.

    That is why the Trapper's chain asks for raw meat rather than cured, and the
    Sapper's for plain cement rather than the reinforced concrete they will later
    own: the good stuff is on the far side of the door you are opening.

    Completing the final stage of a chain rewards that Calling's Writ, which sets
    the Mark CVar when consumed and opens the perk branch. With the Writs removed
    from trader stock, this file is now the ONLY route into a Calling.

    VERIFY-16 (docs/VERIFICATION.md): quest XML is the most structurally complex
    config in the game and the least verifiable without an install. Confirm the
    objective type names (Craft, FetchKeep, AnimalKill, ZombieKill), the reward
    type names (Exp, Quest, Item), and above all HOW A TRADER OFFERS THESE. Quest
    offering has changed across versions; these may need a quest tier or group
    entry, or a traders.xml hook, before they appear at a trader at all.
-->
